We're back with a small update that addresses some of the key requests we've received recently. This update includes adjustments to game mechanics, a rebranding, the addition of a new language, and a few minor tweaks.


 Modification of logo and titles;
 Enemies - [spoiler]One-shot enemies can be stopped during their finish: We noticed some frustration with the 'one-shot' enemies toward the end of the level. Previously, getting caught by one meant instant defeat. We've updated this mechanic to give you the chance to interrupt the attack by killing the NPC, enhancing the cooperative aspect of the game.[/spoiler]
 The Infiltration Agent can use his [spoiler]Stinger gadget to neutralize assistance bots[/spoiler];
 German language added for interface and subtitles;
 Inventory button now on Tab;
 A slight increase in brightness.

We're all ears! We greatly appreciate your valuable feedback, and we want to express our gratitude to those who've shared tips and reported bugs. Your input has been instrumental in shaping this patch, which brings together a myriad of enhancements and bug fixes.

Firstly, it was noted that the combat phases were not quite up to the quality of the puzzles. We decided to improve a few points:

 The feeling of neutralizing enemies has been improved and gives greater satisfaction;
 Enemies are a little more robust, and waves of enemies are denser in some places, allowing for more action and challenge;
 The Infiltration Agent's ammunition pack has been increased to a 16 bullets stack;
 More ammunition boxes during [spoiler]Antik's fight[/spoiler];
 More ammunition boxes before [spoiler]the final boss[/spoiler].


Improvements:

 Increased the range of the Stinger gadget + friendly fire;
 There's no need to fetch [spoiler]the USB key after saving the classic calculator checkpoint at Antikithera[/spoiler], as the document is saved so there's no need to go back and forth;
 Some user feedback improvements for the hacking console;
 Resource boxes/crates no longer reset each time you reload sub-levels;
 Better hints on how to resolve the  [spoiler]galaxy password[/spoiler];
 New hints on how to resolve the [spoiler]first supercapacitor puzzle[/spoiler];
 New hints on how to defuse the first [spoiler]mines[/spoiler];
 Now possible to skip the train & briefing part when in speedrun mode.


New features;

 Mouse inputs can be rebinded;
 Built-in colorblind mode with 3 types of vision deficiencies.


Fixes:

 A few netcode synchronization bugs have been corrected thanks to our observations on Twitch (we always keep an eye to make sure the game is running smoothly);
 Fix softlock on [spoiler]gas cylinders in Terra's ant nest[/spoiler];
 Fix Antik bug where the [spoiler]quantum LEDs were not showing[/spoiler] because of level loading lag on some configs;
 mouse axis inversion no longer disturbs the controllers in [spoiler]the reactor control room[/spoiler];
 Mouse smoothing is now disabled by default in the config files;
 Correction of typos.


Many thanks to all of you!

Dazarious for Questions Factory

We continue to improve the game thanks to the latest feedbacks

Puzzles improvements

 [spoiler] New hint for the Infiltration Agent training section[/spoiler];
 [spoiler] Princeps: we increased the number of possible failures on the galaxy password[/spoiler];
 [spoiler] Antikythera: the crane's camera is more visible[/spoiler];
 [spoiler] Antikythera: the maintenance plate is more visible[/spoiler];
 [spoiler] Antikythera: we added a new hint for the maintenance plate[/spoiler];
 [spoiler] Terra: we increased the nest escape timing[/spoiler];
 [spoiler] Terra: we increased the volume of the Hacker sound cue[/spoiler].


Fixes

 Fixed Terra Badge soft lock;
 Widescreen compatibility: we made adjustments to the layouts, to avoid unwanted distortions, (We will be releasing a new hotfix to make the first person view compatible with 21:9 32:9 ratios (Hor+FoV));
 Stinger: discharge release message now disappears after deactivating [spoiler] a mine[/spoiler].


Other changes
We look for where things can get potentially frustrating and reinforce the weak points.

 We increased the overall brightness of the game;
 Now possible to adjust the FOV in the first person view;
 Increase of the surface illuminated by the flashlight;
 Removed selection lock on respawn;
 Reduced the spread of the shotgun;
 Correction of typos.


Thanks for your feedback ;)

Dazarious for Questions Factory

Fixes

No longer possible to open the inventory when on the loading screen;
Antik [spoiler]LASERs puzzles, no longer possible to pass bewteen vertical LASERs[/spoiler];
Antik [spoiler]fight, no longer possible to sneak behind blocking LASERs[/spoiler].


Other changes

We readjusted the brightness of the flashlight;
Correction of notation:  is now replaced by ;
Princeps area: [spoiler]Fixed game randomization for ventilation puzzle valves[/spoiler];
Correction of typos;
Correction of geometry clipping issues.

We continue the regular process of improving the game thanks to the latest feedbacks

The last patch consisted in improving the combat phases. This time we focused on the puzzles.

Puzzles improvements
Puzzle improvements means that the environment has been changed to accommodate more clues. 
The puzzle has not become simpler, but rather less complex, the path feels "less volatile". Important clues appear better and more info has been added to avoid unnecessary frustration.

 We added several environment clues readable only by the infiltrator to reduce the information processing gap between the two roles ;
 [spoiler]Training - better explanations of the hacking instructions for the DO advanced training[/spoiler] ;
 [spoiler]Security area (scanning machines) - reduction of damage inflicted by turrets[/spoiler] ;
 [spoiler]Security area - the backup generators now have a description[/spoiler] ;
 [spoiler]Princeps area - added some guides on the order in which the main puzzle should be solved[/spoiler] ;
 [spoiler]Princeps area - removed the two nr command arguments that were too confusing[/spoiler] ;
 [spoiler]Centrifuge area - encryption key time window extended[/spoiler] ;
 [spoiler]Centrifuge area - better integration of the clues that show how assisstant bots can be killed[/spoiler] ;
 [spoiler]Antikythera Quantum Area - addition of clues in the documentation, more info about the setup [/spoiler] ;
 [spoiler]Terra decontamination - addition of a new intuitive way to resolve the puzzle[/spoiler] ;
 [spoiler]Control room - generator task, addition of an example in the protocol documentation[/spoiler] ;
 [spoiler]Control room - we fixed some inconveniences of use[/spoiler] ;
 [spoiler]Reactor core (boss fight) - new documentation about how to purge the rods, to avoid having to solve the puzzle by trial and error, which ruined the scene a bit [/spoiler].


Fixes

The game no longer [spoiler]succeed when both players are in unrefueled pods[/spoiler] ;
Quick selection keys (1 2 3 4 line) now working on US keyboards, also possible to rebind them.


Other changes
We look for where things can get potentially frustrating and reinforce the weak points.

 We reduced the clunkyness of the Stinger gadget;
 Improvement of the aiming optics for the assault rifle (red dot reduction);
 Increased attenuation radius of the flashlight;
 Increased the scannable region around the pinpoint of the analyzer (the chances of missing important elements are reduced);
 The base volume of some combat music has been reduced;
 Some puzzle solutions are now randomized only once, the state is now saved for the current game and do not reset after failure;
 Correction of geometry clipping issues;
 Correction of typos.


Thanks for your feedback ;)

Dazarious for Questions Factory

We carefully listen to the feedback you give us, sometimes on the reviews, sometimes on the forum and other times on the streams. 
We try to sort out all the different ideas to get as much improvement as possible without taking away from the original vision of the game. And we have some news!

Major changes
Combat system: some of you have pointed out certain flaws such as an overall clunkyness which was more noticeable during dynamic phases. We have made some improvements and we think that it has smoothed the combat and made it more enjoyable.

 Hit box enhancements for all enemies, the shots are more likely to be successful;
 Action queuing - restored aiming after running if the aiming key is pressed;
 Action queuing - restored aiming after reloading if the aiming key is pressed;
 Action queuing - restored aiming/running after a weapon switch if the corresponding key is pressed;
 Switching between weapons is much faster;
 Faster reloading time for all weapons;
 Increased damage & fire rate for the Infiltration Agent base weapon;
 Increased damage for the Digital Operator weapons;
 Changes in the way damage is received and processed player side (players take longer to die if they have low health);
 We have added medkits between some combat phases;
 Gameplay hints are now given on the reload screen to ensure that you make the most of the features you are given.

Other changes
As always, we are interested in how your operations unfold. We look for where things can get potentially frustrating and reinforce the weak points.

 We have added hints for some puzzles;
 Added a light indicator for one of the Infiltration Agent's gadgets;
 Training - more indications for the advanced training of the Digital Operator;
 Correction of typos;
 Correction of geometry clipping issues;
 The mission briefing is now recalled in the logs.


Thanks for your feedback ;)

Questions Factory

As always, we thank all those who support us in this adventure!

Every day we take a close look at the feedback you give us in order to improve the game experience. So we have detected a few things that needed to be fixed.

Training section
According to your feedback, the training section needed to be improved as it represented an unjustified difficulty. There were also missing explanations in the mini lessons of the tutorial.

 We have improved the training courses by including more explanations about the Infiltration Agent and the gameplay in general;
 We changed the way the Infiltration Agent had to distract the guards;
 For both classes, we removed the mobile guard which was too difficult to manage.

Small fixes

 Default input binding for Move Left is reset to A;
 Default input binding for Trample is reset to Z;
 We corrected some geometry clipping issues;
 Puzzle: [spoiler]Train Station - no longer possible to activate the lever without removing the plate[/spoiler].

Enhancements

 We added some hints for the Princeps area;
 We added one energy station in [spoiler]the registration area (to avoid penalizing those who have no energy from the start)[/spoiler];
 Now possible to quit the external interface of the backpack by pressing the Escape key.

Changes in the EULA: we simply changed the contact email address.

Thank you for all your feedbacks!

Questions Factory
